Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-pyqt6.qtwebengine | python3-pyqt5.qtwebengine | gir1.2-webkit2-4.1, xdg-utils
Recommends: libnotify-bin, pkexec | policykit-1, python3-gi
Suggests: adb
Homepage: https://github.com/jikantoki/LinuxAuto
Description: Android Auto (Google DHU) connection GUI for Ubuntu / Kubuntu
 Linux Auto manages Android Auto connections through Google's Desktop Head
 Unit (DHU) from a simple GUI. It supports USB and Wi-Fi (tethering)
 connections, automatic reconnection and a headunit.ini editor.
 .
 The server runs as a systemd user service (linux-auto.service) and the
 GUI opens in its own window (Qt WebEngine or WebKitGTK).
 .
 Google DHU and adb are not included in this package. Install them from
 the in-app setup guide or with the "linux-auto-setup-sdk" command.
